      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1792, the first planned European American settlement in Livingston County, called Williamsburgh, was established in Groveland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Groveland%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Groveland Shaker Village settlement was founded in 1836 on a 1,700‑acre farm at the hamlet of Sonyea, later becoming the Craig Colony for Epileptics in 1896.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
